            <div xml:id="d779">

                <pb facs="1020" n="906" xml:id="pg906"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.00 Revolutions/8: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Culbertson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-26T16:00:00-05:00">July 26, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>80. Junta consists of President of Senate and Montero and Blanche of last week’s
                    Cabinet. The one uncertain element is still army, which continues loyal to
                    Ibañez, who now announces that he has temporarily withdrawn from office. Crowds
                    have gathered in the main avenue and in front of the Embassy but there are no
                    disorders. No Americans nor American interests have been molested.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
